From 563a38c21a9737757c3e7de4cd3aac7c93800ab4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yekai pan <pyk@seas.upenn.edu>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:14:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 18/24] l2r-local: entry 23-j: worklist release: the tail call
 picks the last dead of two children

Follow-up of 23-i: its tail call took the arm's last deferred member, so
a chain through an earlier member whose last member is a leaf (a
left-deep tree `Node(l, v, Leaf)`, compositions nested on the left, a
closure that captures the next closure and then a fresh one) still went
through a deferral and a pop per level.

Now the release considers the arm's last two such members, a and b. A
candidate is decremented in its place (field order, the answer kept as
an i1 by `deadTest`; an immediate never dies) when no later member may
push work onto the drain (mayPush, 23-i), and, for a, also no member
between a and b; otherwise it is released as the walk releases it,
deferred in its place. After the box's free: if b died, a dead a is
deferred and b's release is tail-called; else a dead a is tail-called.
Earlier such members are deferred as before. So the order is the walk's:
the last child deferred, with nothing pushed after it, is the one that
continues, and the others are popped later, last first.

Instructions per freed cell (microbenchmark, cachegrind, after 23-i /
now): left-deep tree 59.8 / 42.3, left-nested compositions 86.3 / 44.3,
right-deep tree 40.8 / 42.3, 64-arm chain 40.8 / 41.3, balanced tree
50.3 / 52.8, rose tree 51.5 / 48.4 (l2r-base7's retcon drops: 73.3,
109.2, 72.6, 98.6, 57.4, 66.8).

Tests: conversion/worklist_drop.mlir checks the decision (the defer of a
under "b died", the musttail calls of b and of a) and a record whose
member between the two children may push work (a stays deferred in its
place; b continues by a tail call).
