 // Worklist drops release a `RecordDropKind::Worklist` record through the
 // thread's stack of pending drops (reussir-rt's drop_stack.rs), as Lean's
 // lean_del does. Per record type and atomic kind:
-// - `<dtor>.worklist(ref)`, the entry: `reussir.drop.run` of the walk;
+// - `<dtor>.worklist(ref)`, the entry: a variant's leaf arms (no Worklist
+//   box) released in place, the rest `reussir.drop.run` of the walk;
 // - `<dtor>.worklist.walk(ref)`: drops the members in field order, at once,
 //   except member boxes of Worklist records: a box whose count reaches zero
 //   is deferred with `reussir.rc.defer` instead of released by recursion;
 // - `<dtor>.worklist.release(box)`, called by the drain for a deferred box:
-//   the walk of its content, then the box's free.
+//   the content released as by the walk, the box freed, and the last dead
+//   child, if no later member may push work, continued by a tail call (it is
+//   what the drain would pop next).
 // The drain pops the deferred boxes last first. A Worklist value reached
 // through other glue calls its entry, which then only walks (the thread
 // already drains); since glue defers every box edge of its record's cycle,
@@ -35,6 +38,7 @@
 #include <mlir/Dialect/LLVMIR/LLVMAttrs.h>
 #include <mlir/Dialect/LLVMIR/LLVMDialect.h>
